---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_21",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 21,
  "text": "<p> [[107.1]] <b>22. JOHANN VAGETIUS FÜR LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[107.2]] [Hamburg, 7. Dezember 1686.] [23.]</b></p>\n[[107.13]] <b>Clarissimo Dⁿ^#'o Leibnizio ad cogitata per epistolam Dⁿ^#'o Lic. Placcio\n[[107.14]] significata, ferenda a Vagetio, multa cum salute, et paratis officiis,\n[[107.15]] responsa.</b> </p>\n<p> [[107.16]] 1. Logicae schedae Jungianae, quas domi suae habuerat Fogelius, et eo vita functo ad se\n[[107.17]] receperat D. Kirstenius pauloque ante obitum in Bibliothecam publicam transtulerat, descriptae\n[[107.18]] sunt omnes. Apographa earum communicari possunt, consensu Curatorum omnium ut fas est,\n[[107.19]] impetrato, si qua dubitandi ratio occurrit, de loci alicujus scriptura, autographa possunt in\n[[107.20]] bibliotheca inspici, aut, eodem consensu impetrato fortassis aliquando ad breve tempus communicari.\n[[107.21]] Ea in re difficultas nec fuit nec est nec erit, dum certum sit, ita hac in urbe manere\n[[107.22]] quae communicantur, ut repeti quandocunque videtur possint, et non incidere in oculos iniquos\n[[107.23]] autori; et non contineatur in schedis illis aliquid, certas ob causas celandum plane. Consignata\n[[107.24]] enim in aversa parte saepe sunt, quae referebantur de personis quibusdam. Aliter fieri fas,\n[[107.25]] hactenus videri mihi et aliis non potuit, esse. </p>\n<p> [[108.1]] 2. Digestam Dn. Siverus habet Phoranomicam, et illustratam schematibus, moliturque, ut\n[[108.2]] nupera die Dominica, data opera, mihi aperuit, certo nunc editionem. Exstimulare ad accelerandum\n[[108.3]] institutum qui poterit, voletque, bene de Jungio, Sivero et re literaria Mathematica,\n[[108.4]] plane <Fn><i>Darunter am Fuß der Seite von Leibniz' Hand</i>: <i>Textoriam</i> vellem edi.</Fn> credo, merebitur. </p>\n<p> [[108.5]] 3. Ego persevero in describendis per amanuensem schedis, et cum illo relegendis. Digerere\n[[108.6]] coeperam initio, sed, postquam difficultates sine fine objici meis editionibus vidi, desii,\n[[108.7]] idque eo magis, quia pro certo habeo, non posse plerisque melius consuli, quam si, ut jacent,\n[[108.8]] luci dentur omnia, ut cui voluntas et otium est, frui iis possit, aut, si ita placet in corpora\n[[108.9]] quaedam ea concinnare. </p>\n<p> [[108.10]] 4. Heureticam non puto futurum unquam fuisse, ut Jungius Logicae adjiceret, mathesi\n[[108.11]] eam, credo plane, relicturus. </p>\n<p> [[108.12]] 5. Producerentur indies plura, si essent praeter unum atque alterum qui expeterent, aut\n[[108.13]] mihi locus stabilis ubi asservari, dum expeterentur, possent, nec luctandum cum impedimentis\n[[108.14]] paratae pecuniae pro typorum opera tamen objectis. </p>\n<p> [[108.15]] 6. <greek>Metábasiw</i> ad aequivocationem utique recidit, sed est species ejus multa habens\n[[108.16]] peculiaria. Descriptae jam a. 1680 sunt schedae sed mihi hactenus non relectae, relego nunc,\n[[108.17]] nec desinam donec absolvero. Darem typis, nisi desperare successum coepti istius, impedimenta\n[[108.18]] hactenus frequentata propemodum juberent. Apodicticae peculiares sunt <greek>metabásevw</i> ^&!j(+2)\n[[108.19]] aequivocationes ex iis, quae <i>Log. Hamb.</i> IV, III, 6-8 proponuntur subtiliores, ut sphaerae <Fn><i>Zwischen dieser und folgender Zeile von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Ergo <greek>metábasiw</i> fuerit cum usurpamus voces a <greek>F</i>ysico non sensu physico sed Geometrico, v. gr. si sphaeram activitatis interpretamur Geometrice. Sed non puto hunc esse sensum Aristotelis.</Fn>\n[[108.20]] physicae non conveniunt attributa sphaerae stereometricae. </p>\n<p> [[108.21]] 7. Consequentia a rectis quomodo nitatur substitutione terminorum aequipollentium,\n[[108.22]] lubens didicerim. Ego demonstrationem <Fn><i>Darüber von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Ego ibi nullam demonstrationis umbram video.</Fn> ejus video in <i>Log.</i> <Fn><i>Darunter am Fuß der Seite von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Grammatica est ars, Ergo qui discit Grammaticam discit artem. Nam qui discit Grammaticam discit id quod est Grammatica. Qui discit id quod est Grammatica discit id quod est ars. Casus tantum affixis differunt, et possunt distingui articulis sine flexionibus.</Fn> <i>Hamb.</i> III, XXXIII, 1-7. Possunt\n[[109.1]] autem unius rei demonstrationes esse plures, et ex illis alia aliis ingeniis convenientior. Inversam\n[[109.2]] demonstratam characteribus, non expressis verbis, mihi Fogelius olim communicavit,\n[[109.3]] paucis versibus. </p>\n<p> [[109.4]] 8. Homonymia adsignificationis in <i>Log. Hamb.</i> delibata est V, XXX, 9. VI, V, 6. et\n[[109.5]] VII, 19. pleniusque ex ejus schedis et Fogelianis additamentis in Fogelii <i>Lexico Philosophico</i>,\n[[109.6]] quod ex digestis a me ex parte aliqua, unum est, tractata. </p>\n<p> [[109.7]] 9. Exquisitae definitiones ex attributis, attributa ex observatione agnoscendae sunt. Inservit\n[[109.8]] ei rei pro exemplo <i>Isagoge Phytoscopica</i>. Notioni latiori, cum restringentes in re explorata\n[[109.9]] compertu facillimae, adjunguntur, dum reciprocationi quam fieri potest paucissimis verbis,\n[[109.10]] satisfiat, definitio absoluta est. </p>\n<p> [[109.11]] Inquiram autem, cum potero, et, si quid reconditioris sagacitatis reperero, depraedicabo. </p>\n<p> [[109.12]] Quae impressa sunt, ea cupide mittentur, modo jubeatur aliquis a me ea petere, quo\n[[109.13]] oportet transferenda, quem traditurum ea sibi sit expetenti certum. </p>\n",
  "number": "22.",
  "title": "JOHANN VAGETIUS FÜR LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "[Hamburg, 7. Dezember 1686.] [23.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:22. JOHANN VAGETIUS FÜR LEIBNIZ [Hamburg, 7. Dezember 1686.] [23.] Clarissimo Dⁿ^#'o Leibnizio ad cogitata per epistolam Dⁿ^#'o Lic. Placcio significata, ferenda a Vagetio, multa cum salute, et paratis officiis, responsa. 1. Logicae schedae Jungianae, quas domi suae habuerat Fogelius, et eo vita fun...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>